  <result type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved framework conditions for sustainable development</narrative>
   </title>
   <reference code="269652" vocabulary="99"></reference>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="1" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">SSC contributions in 2019 to framework conditions within veterinary and food safety in Colombia: &quot;5 &quot;.

Score from 1-5, 1 lowest and 5 highest.

The planned output targets in the project have been met in 2019.

Several activities were arranged in 2019 covering areas like; Developing a salmonella action plan, Monitoring of residues of drugs and contaminants, High Level Delegation, Risk based control in food and feed, First forum for responsible antimicrobial use, and Rural Development activity.</narrative>
    </title>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2019-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2019-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="5"></target>
     <actual value="5"></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Increase awareness and knowledge of risk based control on the evaluation of hazards and chemical risks in pig meat</narrative>
   </title>
   <reference code="270929" vocabulary="99"></reference>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="1" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Planning and verification mission to Colombia</narrative>
    </title>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="Training visit to Denmark to experience the Danish approach to risk based and need oriented feed and food safety control system"></target>
     <actual value="The DVFA experts proposed to develop a National Control Plan for Colombia based on the principles of the European Multi Annual Nation Control Plan (MANCP). The Colombian authorities agreed that such a plan would be useful and thus, the process started with drafting a national strategy with the objective of improving efficiency of official control for the regulation of food and animal feed via risk-based inspection for all Food Business Operators (importers, manufacturers, etc). The partner authorities ICA and INVIMA agreed on a set of guiding principles for inspection, which was signed at the final Steering Committee Meeting on December 6th 2021."></actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2020-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="Planning and verification mission to Colombia"></target>
     <actual value="The activity was carried out and it was decided to continue the focus on Feed, Food, Veterinary health and Phytosanitary health control with special focus on Multi Annual National Control Plan as well as an introduction to Theory of change"></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">To increase awareness and knowledge on how to reduce salmonella in pig meat through the formulation and implementation of a pathogen reduction plan</narrative>
   </title>
   <reference code="270930" vocabulary="99"></reference>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="1" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Workshop Implementing a pathogen reduction plan</narrative>
    </title>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="Workshop Implementing a pathogen reduction plan"></target>
     <actual value="DVFA and the Colombian partners agreed the Strategic Sector Cooperation should focus on strengthening Colombian authorities&#x2019; ability to develop and implement preventive measures for antibiotic-resistant pathogens reducing salmonella in pork trough formulation and implementation of a national salmonella plan. In 2019, workshops were held to increase awareness and provide knowledge of the Danish experience on how to develop such a plan. One of the recommendations were to establish a cross-institutional technical working group in Colombia, which was later found between authorities and private sector. Here it was agreed that Colombia should seek reducing the prevalence of salmonella in pork an create a national integrated action plan.

It was discussed that Colombia has inadequate knowledge about the presence of this pathogen. Accordingly, it was strategically agreed to invite academia and include a research collaboration project financed by DANIDA with participation of Copenhagen Universi"></actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2020-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="Workshop Implementing a pathogen reduction plan"></target>
     <actual value="Workshop to be conformed"></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
